<title>ITALY: BNL 1996 net profit jumps 15 percent.</title>
<headline>BNL 1996 net profit jumps 15 percent.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     89 vs 77</p>
<p>    Gross profit			   1.23 trln up 34.7 pct</p>
<p>    Ord div				  200 lire vs same</p>
<p>    Savings share div		    1,000 lire vs same</p>
<p>Note - Banca Nazionale del Lavoro said in a statement the results were &quot;satisfactory&quot; against a background of increased competition in the banking sector.</p>
<p>Medium- and long-term loans in the industrial sector rose 3.9 percent and bad debts amounted to 2.16 trillion lire, or 2.6 percent of credits -- slightly up from the 2.4 percent of credits at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>It said interest charges were 2.91 trillion, down two percent, while total charges rose 5.7 percent to 3.2 trillion.</p>
<p>The annual meeting will be held on April 23.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
